 "Avoir": {"z":{"h":"avoir 读音像「阿福哇」→ 阿福什么都有哇！","r":"avoir ← 拉丁 habere（有）；英文 habit、habitat 也来自这个词","s":"想象阿福双手捧着一大堆东西：j'ai 我有、tu as 你有、il a 他有；avoir 里 oi 读「wa」，结尾 r 轻轻带过"},"e":{"h":"sounds like 'av-WAHR' — a pirate shouting 'I HAVE a war chest!'","r":"avoir ← Latin habere (to have); English habit and habitat come from the same root","s":"Picture a pirate hugging his treasure: j'ai, tu as, il a, nous avons, vous avez, ils ont. The oi sounds like 'wa', and the r is soft."}},
